;;; -*- Mode:LISP; Package:USER; Base:10; Readtable:Common-Lisp; Patch-File:T -*-ç;;; Patch directory for Site Data Editor version 8ç;;; Written 19-Nov-87 15:44:30 by pld at site Gigamos Cambridgeç;;; while running on Jack Flanders from band 2ç;;; with Experimental System 123.115, Experimental Local-File 73.2, Experimental FILE-Server 22.1, Experimental Unix-Interface 11.0, Experimental Tape 18.0, Experimental KERMIT 34.0, Experimental ZMail 71.0, Experimental Lambda-Diag 15.0, Experimental Site Data Editor 8.0, microcode 1754, SDU Boot Tape 3.12, SDU ROM 8.çç(:EXPERIMENTALç ((0 "Site Data Editor Loaded" "keith" NIL)ç  (1 "Site Editor converts network numbers and subnet masks to integers when read fromçsite files, and back to human-readable form when writing to site files.çAlways stored as numbers when in memory for easy comparisons." "pld" NIL)ç  (2 "When you flush the database, clear the current item from the window.çWhen you delete the currently edited object, clear it from window.çSpeed up the :delete-all-items method (delete from end, rather than topçof list -- no more scrolling!)çThe :site-option initialization now calls (flush-database) ratherçthan (forget-buffered-data), so when you reload the site filesçyour current object is cleared." "pld" NIL)ç  (3 "When the Site Editor is in Expert Mode, the command menu does not include theçcomments.  If you then recompile a menu command, the frame is asked toçrecompute its menu, and you end up with the comments.  Slight change to theç:sort-menu-commands methods fixes this." "pld" NIL)ç  (4 "The Site Editor doesn't allow you to assign addresses that are not on knownçnetworks.  Unfortunately, it wasn't taking subnet masks into account.çDitto when checking whether a network number was in use when definingçnew networks." "pld" NIL)ç  ))